# TIRO alone, SPACE held for 3 s with Windows' key repeat (BUGS.md T1, T3).
#
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame tiro --headless --ms 30000 --key-repeat 500,33 --input tools/play/tiro-endless.input
#   zig-out/bin/noite --minigame tiro --headless --ms 30000 --key-repeat 500,33 --fix all --input tools/play/tiro-endless.input
#
# (500,33 is the default of every run; the flag makes the script independent
# of it.) No result in either version:
# - Original: the press and its repeats (from 500 ms, every 33 ms) each
#   take an arrow (T1, T2): `lives` drops about 3 per 100-ms target tick, so
#   no tick sees it at exactly 1 (T3), it goes negative and TIRO never ends.
# - `--fix all`: the latch holds the repeats off (T1): one shot, 15 arrows
#   left, and the game ends only when none is left (T4): it goes on.
